    "created_at": "2019-10-16T13:20:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-10-16T13:20:11Z",
    "body": "The action is largely intended for allowing content editable elements to be able to customize the enter key. So it makes sense for it to be on the element, as in those cases there is no form control. It merely dispatches an enter key at the element in question. Whether that causes a form submit has a number of conditionals on it. A textarea inside a form doesn't. A form that doesn't have all the require entries filled in won't be submitted etc. Also specifying it on the form prevents you from customizing it for individual controls without additional javascript.\r\n\r\nFor these reasons I don't believe it should be on the form element.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
