    "created_at": "2019-10-16T16:53:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-10-16T16:53:15Z",
    "body": "I'm not denying the usefulness of having the attribute on individual elements, but wondering about the utility of having it on the form as well as a default for elements within the form, rather than requiring it to be specified on every input element.\r\n\r\nI presume the UA would always be able to override the hint for cases where the form fails validation, etc. and won't be submitted by an enter.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
